Hi,

I'm new to ggplot2 and this group so first off, if this sort of post is inappropriate here, please do let me know.  I very much like the idea of using a summary statistic to plot a confidence interval directly from a dataset without needing to use dplyr to generate that confidence interval.  I found a great example of how to do this on StackOverflow <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32669473/plotting-the-means-with-confidence-intervals-with-ggplot>, and I paste the code at the end of this question.  My problem is that this code works great with: ggplot2_0.9.3.1 and Hmisc_3.14-0, but when I run it with ggplot2_2.2.0 and Hmisc_3.17-1, I get this error:   Error: Unknown parameters: width, conf.int <http://conf.int>

I have a two part questions.
1) Why am I getting this error and how do I fix it?
2) As a newbie, how am I supposed to figure out the cause of this error on my own?

For #2, I tried looking in the documentation for geom_ribbon and stat_summary in both the old and new ggplot2 and I just don't see any mention of conf.int <http://conf.int>.  So how am I supposed to figure out how the old ribbon geometry used conf.int <http://conf.int> and why the new version of ribbon doesn't seem to recognize it?  Is the best strategy for me to learn about the guts of ggplot2 and dig into the code itself?  If so, how should I begin?  I have Hadley's book from about 2010, but I don't think it goes this deep into things and it's maybe outdated too for ggplot2_2.2.0.

Andy

# sample data - should be provided in question
set.seed(1)      # for reproducible example
time <- 1:25
df   <- data.frame(time,
                   pop=rnorm(100*length(time), mean=10*time/(25+time)))

library(ggplot2)
ggplot(df, aes(x=time, y=pop))+
  stat_summary(geom="ribbon", fun.data=mean_cl_normal, width=0.1, conf.int <http://conf.int>=0.95, fill="lightblue")+
  stat_summary(geom="line", fun.y=mean, linetype="dashed")+
  stat_summary(geom="point", fun.y=mean, color="red")

